// @expect-error 'shown<Handle>' cannot interpolate a value of type 'Handle': an external type has no text form. Pass a type argument that has a text form, or the text you want instead.
// @expect-note 'shown<T>' interpolates a value of type 'T' here
// @expect-error 'isSpeaker<Voice>' cannot use 'is' on a value of type 'Voice', because only a class value can be tested with 'is'. 'Voice' implements 'Speaker', but a struct value is never a class instance. Pass a class that implements 'Speaker' instead.
// @expect-note 'isSpeaker<T>' tests a value of type 'T' against 'Speaker' here
